Mental health should be given due importance to improve the quality of life. Argue.', 'Outline (800-word essay):
Introduction - The WHO defines mental health as a state of wellbeing in which a person can cope with normal stresses, work productively and contribute to the community. Mental health deserves the same importance as physical health because quality of life depends on both.
Arguments - Good mental health shapes how we think, feel, learn, work and relate to others; poor mental health lowers productivity, damages relationships and worsens physical illness. In Bhutan, rising stress, depression, substance abuse and suicide, especially among young people, show the cost of neglect. Stigma stops many from seeking help. The economy loses when people cannot work or study well, and families and communities suffer. Psychological wellbeing is a domain of Gross National Happiness, so caring for the mind is part of our national vision.
Suggestions - Awareness campaigns to reduce stigma; trained counsellors in every school and college; accessible mental health services and helplines; workplace wellbeing policies; strong family and community support; healthy habits, mindfulness and meditation drawn from our own traditions.
Conclusion - Giving mental health due importance improves individual happiness, family life and national productivity; it is essential for a good quality of life.', null, '[{"point": "Introduction: what mental health is (WHO) and a clear stand that it deserves equal importance with physical health", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Arguments: mental health shapes wellbeing, relationships, learning and productivity; links to physical health; rising problems (stress, depression, substance use, suicide) among youth in Bhutan", "marks": 9}, {"point": "Arguments: economic and social costs; stigma prevents help-seeking; GNH psychological wellbeing domain; examples", "marks": 9}, {"point": "Suggestions: awareness, school counselling, services and helplines, workplace wellbeing, family/ community support, mindfulness", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Conclusion restating the argument", "marks": 3}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-language'),
