  values ('ME', 'essay', 'Write an essay in about 800 words on the following topic. (Assessed on thought and content development 15, communicative competence and vocabulary 10, grammatical accuracy and variety 5.) (30 marks)

Quality civil service is the call of the time when the country is undergoing transformation. Discuss.', 'Outline (800-word essay):
Introduction - Bhutan is undergoing a major transformation under His Majesty''s guidance: civil service and education reforms, the 13th Five Year Plan, digital governance and Gelephu Mindfulness City. The civil service is the engine that turns these visions into results.
Why quality matters - Civil servants design and implement policies, deliver education, health and other services, and build public trust. Weak performance, red tape and the loss of skilled officers through resignation and emigration slow national progress, so quality is no longer optional.
What a quality civil service looks like - Competent, professional officers selected and promoted on merit; performance-based management and accountability; integrity and transparency; efficient, digital and citizen-centred services; innovation and a willingness to take responsibility.
How to achieve it - Continue the reforms (restructuring, performance management, leadership development); invest in training and technology; reward excellence and retain talent; uphold the values of the Tsa-Wa-Sum and GNH.
Conclusion - At this time of transformation, a high-quality civil service is essential for Bhutan to realise its vision of a developed, happy and self-reliant nation.', null, '[{"point": "Introduction: national transformation (His Majesty''s vision, civil service reform, 13th FYP, GMC, digital economy) and the civil service''s central role", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Why quality matters: implements policies, delivers services, drives economy and trust; challenges (attrition/ emigration, bureaucracy, low productivity)", "marks": 9}, {"point": "What quality means: competence and professionalism, meritocracy and performance management, integrity and accountability, efficiency and digital service delivery, citizen-centred, innovation", "marks": 9}, {"point": "How to achieve it: reforms (RCSC restructuring, performance management), training and leadership development, technology, retention and motivation, values (Tsa-Wa-Sum)", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Conclusion", "marks": 3}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-language'),
