  values ('ME', 'passage', 'Question II. 3) "''One size fits all'' approach in education negatively affects the learning experiences of diverse students, particularly those with disabilities." Justify. (5 marks)', 'A ''one size fits all'' approach gives every learner the same content, pace, teaching method and test. Learners are different: a child with a hearing or visual impairment cannot follow a lecture or a blackboard without support; a slow learner needs more time; a learner whose home language differs needs language help. When these needs are ignored, such students fall behind, lose confidence, feel excluded and may drop out, while gifted learners are not challenged. Inclusive education instead uses differentiated instruction, teaching aids, assistive technology and flexible assessment, so that every learner, including those with disabilities, can learn and succeed.', null, '[{"point": "Explains ''one size fits all'': same content, pace, methods and assessment for every learner", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Justification with effects on diverse learners/ disabilities: needs ignored, barriers (sight, hearing, language), falling behind, low confidence, exclusion/ dropout; contrast with differentiated/ inclusive teaching", "marks": 3.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-language'),
