  values ('ME', 'descriptive', 'Read the information given below carefully and write a précis in not more than 100 words: in one paragraph, including the main points, with a short title. (20 marks)

The modern era is the era of machines. Robots, now, perform many duties starting from mopping the floor to flying an aeroplane. This, in turn, resulted in a heated debate that a sedentary style of living is the primary cause of the plethora of diseases. I completely agree with this notion due to the following reasons.

Firstly, I think that humans need some leisure time to ponder over more serious issues. But the irony of the fact is that people have started rely more on machinery. Automation tools rendered men work less, which has eventually given birth to the vast majority of diseases. For example, a sedentary lifestyle is one of the top causes of death and disability in today’s world. It leads to obesity, which in turn burdens us with physical, social, psychological, and emotional problems.

Secondly, I am of the view that machine should be used as a tool, not an end-point. It should not make us handicapped. As it is said, “The more you grind your body, the more it shines”; hardworking with minimal help of modern technology is the need of the hour. Reducing our time of sitting before television or computers is a standout example of countering sedentary living. In this respect, we have to be very clear about drawing a line between passive entertainment and active recreation.

In conclusion, a mundane lifestyle is unquestionably one of the most prevailing and worrying aspects in current society. The time has come that we should now come out of our ivory towers and experience real life. Participation in social welfare activities is an efficacious cure for the problems created by a sedentary lifestyle.', 'Title: The Cost of a Sedentary Life
In today''s machine age, robots and automated tools perform tasks from cleaning floors to flying aircraft, making people physically inactive. The writer agrees that this sedentary lifestyle is the main cause of many diseases. Over-reliance on machines reduces physical work and leads to obesity, which brings physical, social, psychological and emotional problems and is a leading cause of death and disability. Machines should remain tools that assist us, not make us helpless. People should limit time spent before televisions and computers, choose active recreation over passive entertainment, and take part in social welfare activities to counter the ill effects of inactivity. (98 words)', null, '[{"point": "Suitable short title", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Machines/ robots now do most work, leading to sedentary lifestyles - a main cause of many diseases (writer agrees)", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Over-reliance on automation reduces physical work; sedentary living causes obesity and physical, social, psychological problems", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Machines should be tools, not replace effort; reduce screen time, prefer active recreation; social welfare activities as cure", "marks": 5}, {"point": "One paragraph, own words, within 100 words, correct language", "marks": 4}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-language'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'english-language') and t.slug = 'precis-writing'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-bed-2'), 'standard', 20,
    2160, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
